# 11. RECOVERY ENGINE

Audit transaction recovery.

A recovery system must not blindly repeat mutations.

It should classify transactions based on actual evidence.

Example:

| Evidence | Decision |
|---|---|
| No durable intent and no side effects | Safe to start |
| Intent exists, no business effects | Resume or safely abort |
| All required effects verified | COMMITTED |
| Some effects verified | RECOVERY_REQUIRED |
| Timeout and outcome unknown | UNKNOWN |
| Duplicate effects detected | RECOVERY_REQUIRED |
| Source record exists, downstream effects missing | RECOVERY_REQUIRED |
| Reversal/compensation verified | RECONCILED |

Repair recovery logic if needed.

Recovery must:
- Be idempotent.
- Be safe after restart.
- Avoid duplicate business effects.
- Avoid silent transaction deletion.
- Preserve audit history.
- Avoid restoring old business records.

If automated recovery could cause damage, stop and require controlled manual reconciliation.

